# Aura inherited transport configuration (not activated target role routing).
#
#   cp .env.example .env     then fill in the values in .env
#
# .env is git-ignored and must stay that way. This file carries NAMES ONLY and
# never a value — if you ever find a real key here, it has been committed and
# must be rotated, not deleted. DEC-010 states the same rule; audit F13 found this
# file shipping two model ids anyway, while README.md and CURRENT_STATE.md both
# claimed no model id was committed to source. Values belong in .env.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the test suite: every test injects a fake
# transport, and no test may make a live model call. These matter only when you
# start making real calls.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the providers you actually route to need a key. A missing key fails
# closed at call time, naming the variable it wanted.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
KIMI_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model selection — per capability
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model ids are configuration, never code: there is no in-code default, so an
# unset variable stops the call rather than reaching for a stale identifier.
# These are inherited capability bindings. See AURA_ARCHITECTURE.md for the
# target roles; role-specific production wiring remains unimplemented.
#
# These are keyed on the CAPABILITY, not the provider. Two capabilities may route
# to the same provider and still need different models — ROUTINE_AUDIT and
# EXEC_DEBUG both route to Moonshot. Audit F11 found the previous provider-keyed
# arrangement collapsing them onto one variable, which left AUDITOR_MODEL
# unreachable by anything while this file documented it as the review seat.

# HIGH_REASONING — Architect and final-gate audit.
ARCHITECT_MODEL=

# ROUTINE_AUDIT — per-packet review. Must differ in family from the builder;
# ModelProvider.audit_call enforces that structurally, not by configuration.
AUDITOR_MODEL=

# CODING — the builder seat.
BUILDER_MODEL=

# FAST — scoping, classification, routing.
FAST_MODEL=

# EXEC_DEBUG — sandbox execution and test-fix loops.
EXEC_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model selection — cross-family audit fallbacks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When the candidate was produced by the same family that normally audits the
# capability, independent_auditor reroutes the audit to another family, and the
# capability's own model id is meaningless there. Each provider therefore names
# the model it serves when it is pulled in as a substitute auditor.
#
# Set only the ones whose families you actually route to. Leaving one unset makes
# that reroute fail closed and name the variable, which is the intended behaviour:
# before F11 the fallback silently borrowed ARCHITECT_MODEL, turning a cheap
# per-packet review into a final-gate call with nothing in the receipt to show it.

ANTHROPIC_AUDIT_MODEL=
OPENAI_AUDIT_MODEL=
GEMINI_AUDIT_MODEL=
KIMI_AUDIT_MODEL=
DEEPSEEK_AUDIT_MODEL=
